## Honest scoreboard

* No leaf inhabited. The research count stays at five leaves / six lemmas, and
  the frozen rows A–D stay open.
* Progress claimed, against the round metric: a previously absent literal
  physical object was constructed (the lattice inverse propagator, in the
  repository's own syntax) and a uniform quantitative estimate was proved on
  it; the estimation machinery it feeds is now proved sound rather than
  asserted by placeholder fields; and one premise — full-state RG contraction
  — was eliminated in favour of a strictly weaker observed-fibre premise.
* Not claimed: any inhabited one-loop *density* (the numerators are still
  missing), any closure of A1, any change to the Clay-facing endpoint
  theorems.

## Suggested next step

Lane A1a, unchanged in priority: write the actual momentum-space Wilson,
Faddeev–Popov and Haar *numerators* in the existing syntax — the denominator is
now done — together with atom bound tables valid on the regular region, and run
them through the calculus proved here. Either the derived weighted bound comes in under 44/3 and the
lane advances materially, or it does not and the obstruction becomes visible
immediately.
